WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:08.000
"Tumu Matu'a y Omotohi" — Root of the Ancestors
Performed by Agrupación Cultural Mana Ma'ohi

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:18.000
[A traditional Rapa Nui chant invoking the ancestral origins
of the island's people — the voyagers who crossed the Pacific]

3
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:30.000
[Mana Ma'ohi — "Indigenous spiritual power"
The performers channel mana through voice, rhythm, and movement]

4
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:42.000
[These ríu — sacred songs — carry centuries
of Rapa Nui history, knowledge, and tradition]

5
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:52.000
[Rapa Nui, one of Earth's most remote inhabited islands,
where fewer than 3,000 speakers keep the language alive]

6
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.000
[A voice from the Pacific —
still chanted, still remembered]
